course: dictionary
lesson: 13320
title: Grouping
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A grouping is a set of people or things that are put together because they are alike or work together. «We sorted the animals into groupings: birds, fish and insects.» Each grouping has things that share a feature, so you can see the sorting at once.
explain: Grouping can also be a verb. To group means to put things into groups. «The teacher grouped the pupils into teams of four.» Here grouping is the act of sorting, and grouped is what the teacher did.
explain: In maths, grouping means putting objects or numbers into equal groups to help you count, multiply or divide. «Three groups of 4 make 12.» Read the sentence and ask: how many groups are there, and how many are in each one?
fact: Grouping means putting things into sets that are alike or work together.
fact: Group can be a noun or a verb: a group of pupils, or to group the pupils.
fact: In maths, «3 groups of 4» means 4 + 4 + 4, which makes 12.
fact: Grouping in tens helps you count big numbers: 30 is three groups of ten.
fact: In science, grouping animals or materials by their features is a key skill.
exercise: «We sorted the animals into groupings: birds, fish and insects.» What does grouping mean here? | Losing things on a trip | Drawing a picture of a zoo | Counting backwards from ten | *A set of things put together because they are alike
exercise: «Put 12 counters into 3 equal groups.» What does grouping help you do in maths? | *Share or multiply into equal groups | Find a country on a map | Read a poem aloud | Paint a picture
exercise: The teacher ___ the pupils into teams for the project. Choose the right word. | grip | grown | *grouped | grow
test: «Ability grouping puts pupils into sets by how well they learn.» In ability grouping, what is put together? | The teachers' names | *Pupils who learn at a similar level | The weather on the day | Books and pencils
test: In science we sorted leaves by shape and size. What was the grouping? | Taking the leaves outside to dry | Naming the leaves after people | Feeding the leaves to the class | *Putting the leaves into groups by their features
exam: What is 3 groups of 4? | *12 | 1 | 7 | 34
